.TH NEOMOUSE 1 "2026-07-27" "neomouse 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
neomouse \- Vim\-motion keyboard\-driven mouse control daemon for macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neomouse
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B neomouse
is a macOS menu\-bar daemon that intercepts keyboard events via a global
.B CGEventTap
and translates Vim motions into mouse movements, clicks, scrolls, and
gestures.
It runs in the background with no Dock icon; a mode\-colored status icon
appears in the menu bar.
.PP
The interaction model is mode\-based, mirroring Vim.
On launch the daemon enters the mode specified by
.I mode_on_start
in
.I settings.toml
(default:
.BR normal ).
.TP
.B normal
.B hjkl
moves the cursor.
Numeric counts (e.g.\&
.BR 5j )
and motions
.RB ( gg ,
.BR G ,
.BR 0 ,
.BR $ )
are supported.
.B s
snaps to the nearest ruler cell.
Capital
.B H\|J\|K\|L
scrolls.
.B Ctrl\-w
followed by
.B hjkl
jumps between displays.
.B m{a\-z}
sets a mark;
.BI ' {a\-z}
and
.BI ` {a\-z}
jump back to it.
.BI \" {reg}
selects a register.
.B ?
opens the help dialog.
.TP
.B find
A labelled grid overlay covers the screen.
One or two keypresses warps the cursor to the chosen cell.
.TP
.B specialFind
A small grid appears around the current cursor position.
A single keypress lands on the picked cell.
.BR q / w / e / r
nudge the cursor ±10 pts.
.TP
.B visual
Entered with
.BR v .
Movement extends a highlighted selection rectangle.
.B y
yanks (screenshot via
.BR ScreenCaptureKit ).
Register round\-trips
.RB ( """ay ,
.BR """ap ,
\&...)
work with real
.B NSPasteboardItem
values.
.TP
.B command
.B :
opens a command\-line overlay with fuzzy\-filtered suggestions
.RB ( numbers ,
.BR relativenumbers ,
.BR delmarks ,
.BR restart ,
\&...).
.B Tab
/
.B Shift\-Tab
and
.B Ctrl\-n
/
.B Ctrl\-p
cycle through matches.
.TP
.B menu
A keyboard\-navigable marks browser and a Pasty\-style register browser.
.TP
.B disabled
The event tap is in listen\-only mode.
Every keypress passes straight through to the focused application.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Runtime tuning is stored in
.BR settings.toml ,
a TOML file validated against
.B schema/settings.schema.json
at load time.
.PP
Configuration is resolved once at startup.
The first path that exists wins:
.TP
1.
.B $NEOMOUSE_CONFIG
\(em full path to an alternate
.I settings.toml
(overrides everything when set).
.TP
2.
.B ~/.config/neomouse/settings.toml
\(em the standard per\-user location.
On first launch,
.B neomouse
copies its bundled default
.I settings.toml
here if no file is already present.
.TP
3.
.B ~/Library/Application\ Support/neomouse/settings.toml
\(em macOS\-native fallback.
.PP
Properties in
.B NeoMouseState
fall back to compiled\-in defaults when no settings file is resolved.
.PP
The schema enforces strict key validation: unknown TOML keys and unknown
enum values are rejected at decode time and surfaced as a toast notification.
.PP
Notable configuration sections:
.TP
.B [grid]
Find\-mode overlay divisions, label alphabets, and inner\-character display.
.TP
.B [motion]
.I rows_on_screen
/
.I columns_on_screen
(integer or
.BR \(dqautomatic\(dq )
and cursor\-clamping behaviour.
.TP
.B [visual]
.I minimum_highlight_width
for the selection rectangle.
.TP
.B [gesture]
Pinch/zoom step value, scroll increments, and rotation degrees.
.TP
.B [commands]
Whitelist of commands available in the
.B command
mode overlay.
.TP
.B [configuration]
.I mode_on_start ,
.I is_disable_key_input ,
.I is_show_key_cast ,
.I is_auto_snap ,
.I max_session_count ,
and related behavioural knobs.
.TP
.B [theme.*]
Per\-element visual overrides for every overlay.
Nine sub\-sections:
.BR theme.grid ,
.BR theme.numbers_overlay ,
.BR theme.command_line ,
.BR theme.marks_menu ,
.BR theme.register_menu ,
.BR theme.help_dialog ,
.BR theme.visual_highlight ,
.BR theme.toast ,
and
.BR theme.key_cast .
Colors are hex strings
.RB ( #rrggbb
or
.BR #rrggbbaa );
fonts are inline tables with
.IR family ,
.IR size ,
.IR weight ,
and
.I design
fields.
.PP
Theme and behaviour changes can also be applied without restarting:
.B neomouse
watches the resolved
.I settings.toml
for writes (debounced 250\ ms, atomic\-save aware) and reloads automatically.
The
.B Settings\&...
item in the menu\-bar dropdown (or
.B \(aqCommand+,\(aq
when neomouse is focused) opens a native preferences window where controls
apply live and
.B \(aqCommand+S\(aq
persists changes to disk.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $NEOMOUSE_CONFIG
User\-defined override path (environment variable).
.TP
.B ~/.config/neomouse/settings.toml
Primary per\-user configuration file.
Auto\-populated from the bundled defaults on first launch.
.TP
.B ~/Library/Application\ Support/neomouse/settings.toml
macOS\-native fallback configuration path.
.TP
.B ~/Library/Logs/neomouse/neomouse.log
Runtime log file (written automatically when running from a bundled
.IR .app ).
Accessible via
.B Diagnostics\ \(->\ Show\ Debug\ Log
in the menu\-bar dropdown, or directly in
.BR Console.app .
.SH PERMISSIONS
.PP
.B neomouse
requires two macOS privacy permissions, both granted in
.BR "System Settings \(-> Privacy & Security" :
.TP
.B Accessibility
Required for the global
.B CGEventTap
to intercept and synthesize keyboard and mouse events.
macOS prompts on first launch; click
.I Allow
and relaunch
.BR neomouse .
.TP
.B Input Monitoring
Required to read raw key events from physical input devices while other
applications are focused.
Grant the same way as Accessibility, then relaunch.
.PP
Until both permissions are granted the event tap cannot install and
.B neomouse
will not be able to intercept keyboard input.
